<!-- CONVERTED — VISUALLY VERIFIED --><chapter xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" xml:id="ch05-differentiation-rules-and-elementary-functions">
  <title>Differentiation Rules and Elementary Functions</title>
  <shorttitle>Differentiation Rules</shorttitle>

  <introduction><p>Differentiation rules let us find derivatives without evaluating the defining limit each time. This chapter develops rules for sums, products, quotients, compositions, implicit relations, and inverse functions, then applies them to the elementary functions. The appropriate rule depends on how the function is formed and where it is defined.</p></introduction>

